base {
    A base is a container for ideas, ideasets, and files.
    It forms the boundary of one ideas graph and is consumed by the CLI and the extension.
    Marker: a directory is a base only when it owns a `.reqlan` folder ([app_memory_doc.application_memory]).
    No bare workspace folder is treated as a base until the user creates `.reqlan` there
    ([create_base_onboarding]).
    Aligns with [ontology_base].
    Discovery and registry: [base_discovery], [base_registry].
    Marker path helpers: [application_memory_impl].
    @implementation (
        [base_discovery]
        [base_registry]
        [application_memory_impl]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:returns empty when no .reqlan exists"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:discovers base at workspace root"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:skips node_modules and does not treat .reqlan as a walkable base root"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:isPathInsideOrEqual treats Windows drive paths as case-insensitive"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/application-memory.test.ts:defaults to <workspace>/.reqlan"]
    )


}



base_ownership {
    Each base holds its own [ideas_index] store under `<base>/.reqlan/ideas-index.sqlite`.
    Path keys inside the index are relative to that base root, not the VS Code workspace root.
    Store path: [application_memory_impl]; per-base engine: [workspace_index] via [base_registry].
    @implementation (
        [application_memory_impl]
        [workspace_index]
        [base_registry]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/application-memory.test.ts:defaults to <workspace>/.reqlan"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/application-memory.test.ts:honours storagePath override"]
    )
}

base_configuration {
    Base configuration is distinct from, but related to, [extension_configuration].
    Optional settings live at `<base>/.reqlan/config.json` (one config per base).
    For an `.rq` file, the applying base is the nearest ancestor that owns `.reqlan`; that base's config applies when present.
    See [extension_configuration.configuration_location]; resolved by [path_resolve].
    @implementation (
        [path_resolve]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/language/test/config.test.ts:returns undefined when no config exists"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/config.test.ts:loads config from the owning base .reqlan"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/config.test.ts:loads config from an ancestor base"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/config.test.ts:nearest base config wins over farther ones"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/config.test.ts:owning base without config does not inherit parent"]
        ["../../packages/language/test/path-resolve.test.ts:loads importRoots list from nearest base config"]
    )
}

base_configuration_provider {
    Base-level settings live at `<base>/.reqlan/config.json`.
    Extension-level settings remain VS Code configuration for the product host.
    @implementation (
        [application_memory_impl]
        [path_resolve]
        ["../../packages/extension/schemas/config.schema.json"]
    )
}

base_nesting {
    Bases may nest: any subdirectory that owns its own `.reqlan` is a child base.
    Parent-base indexing includes only `.rq` files under the parent root that are **not** under
    any child base root ([base_discovery] ownership exclusion).
    Nested bases appear as siblings in the multi-base registry; the longest-matching base root
    wins for a given file path ([implied_context]).
    @implementation (
        [base_discovery]
        [base_registry]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:discovers nested bases and excludes child files from parent ownership"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:baseForPath picks longest matching root"]
    )
}
base_linking {
    A base may have one-directional relationships with other bases.
    This follows a subscription model.
    Bases may be cross subscribed.
    Unless linked, than bases remain isolated.
    Base linking is configured in the config file in the base .reqlan directory.
    - an unlinked child base should sever the contained ideas from the parent base (i.e. the parent should just see the child as a separate base and child ideas shouldn't be visible, the indexer shouldn't crawl it.) they should be functionally distinct
    - bases, distinct from eachother in the system file tree, should be linkeable (either one way or both ways)
    - A linked child base should allow the parent base to see the child's ideas. The indexs should be linked, and the child counts etc should be included in the parents.
    - A child base should always be able to link to parent base ideas.
    @todo
}
base_modes {
    A base may be linked to 
    @todo   
}

base_initialisation {
    Bases are initialised with `<base>/.reqlan/config.json`, `.reqlan/.rqignore` (gitignore-syntax path filters; see [extension_configuration.configuration_rqignore]), `.reqlan/.gitignore` ([base_initialisation_ignore]), and a sqlite ideas index under `.reqlan` ([base_ownership]).
    [create_base_impl] creates the `.reqlan` marker and seeds a minimal `config.json`, default `.rqignore` (["../extension/module/index.rq".rqignore_initialisation]), and `.gitignore` when the base is new.
    Full install sequencing (extension welcome vs base seeds vs agent files): ["../extension/installation.rq".base_installation].
}

base_initialisation_ignore {
    New bases seed `<base>/.reqlan/.gitignore` so Git does not track SQLite application-memory files.
    Patterns cover the ideas index ([base_ownership]), the diagnostics store ([app_memory_doc.index_diagnostics_store]), and SQLite sidecars (`*.sqlite`, `*.sqlite-journal`, `*.sqlite-shm`, `*.sqlite-wal`).
    This file is Git ignore for `.reqlan/`. Path filters for discovery stay in `.rqignore` ([extension_configuration.configuration_rqignore] / [app_memory_doc.rqignore]).
    Written by [create_base_impl] as part of [base_initialisation] / ["../extension/installation.rq".base_installation].
    @implementation (
        [create_base_impl]
        ["../../packages/analytical/src/core/application-memory.ts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/ignore.rs"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/create-base.test.ts:seeds .reqlan/.gitignore that excludes sqlite artifacts"]
        ["../../crates/reqlan-index/src/ignore.rs:create_base_seeds_gitignore_for_sqlite_artifacts"]
    )
    @status done
}

implied_context {
    The **active base** for editor-adjacent surfaces is the longest-matching base root that
    contains the focused file path. When no file is focused, the last selected base (Ideas Summary
    switcher / activity bar) or the first discovered base is used.
    Context, local graph, and analysers bind to the active base's index — not a merged global graph.
    User/explicit pin is a pointer swap only — [active_base_switch].
    Core selection: [base_discovery] (`baseForPath` / `selectDefaultBase`); editor pin/switch: [editor_index_adapter].
    @implementation (
        [base_discovery]
        [editor_index_adapter]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:baseForPath picks longest matching root"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:selectDefaultBase prefers cwd containment"]
    )
}

active_base_switch {
    Changing the active base is a **pointer swap** onto a per-base `WorkspaceIndex` / store.
    - Do **not** await soft-sync, hard-rebuild, or a full `.rq` walk on the switch call itself.
    - Host surfaces rebind views to the newly active store (status snapshot, tables, context panes) immediately.
    - If the selected base is not yet ready, show its readiness/progress and **schedule** the normal activate catch-up
      (open if needed, then one soft sync) fire-and-forget — same path as ["../indexer/indexer.rq".triggers] /
      ["../extension/features-graph-analysers.rq".indexing_trigger_open], not a special switcher rebuild.
    - Idle staleness checks only touch bases that are already open; they must not reopen every discovered base
      (["../extension/sqlite-artifact-lifecycle.rq".release_when_idle]).
    - Open failures stay isolated per base so one bad base cannot leave siblings stranded in `uninitialized`.
    - Editor-follow must not overwrite a user pin on the same refresh that applies the selection.
    - Inactive bases release SQLite artifacts when the active pointer moves away
      (["../extension/sqlite-artifact-lifecycle.rq".sqlite_artifact_lifecycle]).
    Surfaces: activity bar ["../extension/module/activitybar-panels/workspace.rq".workspace_base_picker], Ideas Summary ["../extension/module/ideas_summary/base-scope.rq".ideas_summary_base_scope].
    Implemented by [editor_index_adapter] (`setActiveBaseId` / `scheduleBaseCatchUp`); engine: [base_registry] `ensureBaseReady` / `releaseArtifacts`, [workspace_index] `ensureReady` / `deactivate`.
    @implementation (
        [editor_index_adapter]
        [base_registry]
        [workspace_index]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/activity-bar-webview-provider.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/webview_module/ideas-summary-panel.ts"]
        ["../extension/module/activitybar-panels/workspace.rq".workspace_base_picker]
        ["../extension/module/ideas_summary/base-scope.rq".ideas_summary_base_scope]
        ["../extension/sqlite-artifact-lifecycle.rq".sqlite_artifact_lifecycle]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-catchup.test.ts:ensureBaseReady opens and soft-syncs an uninitialized base"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-catchup.test.ts:checkStaleAll heals an uninitialized base"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-catchup.test.ts:deactivate returns to uninitialized so a base can be reopened"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/sqlite-artifact-release.test.ts:BaseRegistry releaseArtifacts closes handles but keeps descriptors"]
    )
    @status done
}

multi_base_environment {
    Analytical features are multibase aware via [base_registry]:
    one [ideas_index] / `WorkspaceIndex` per base, isolated catalogs (no cross-base idea-id collision).
    Surfaces list all discovered bases; Ideas Summary and context panes scope to the active/selected base ([active_base_switch]).
    Cross-base reference resolution and merged graphs are out of scope for the first multi-base pass.
    Headless (CLI/MCP) selects one base via [analysis_runtime]; the editor hosts [editor_index_adapter].
    @implementation (
        [base_registry]
        [base_discovery]
        [editor_index_adapter]
        [analysis_runtime]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:discovers nested bases and excludes child files from parent ownership"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:baseForPath picks longest matching root"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:selectDefaultBase prefers cwd containment"]
    )
}

create_base_onboarding {
    When discovery finds **zero** bases under any VS Code workspace folder (root or child),
    the extension prompts the user to create a reqlan base at the workspace-folder root.
    Do not auto-create `.reqlan`. Command `reqlan.createBase` creates `<folder>/.reqlan/`
    (empty directory is a valid marker) via [create_base_impl], then calls [refresh_bases_pass]
    so the new marker is registered and the returned [base] descriptor matches discovery.
    With multiple workspace folders and no bases, prompt against the first folder.
    Headless create-base helper: [create_base_impl] (also used by CLI `init`).
    @implementation (
        [create_base_impl]
        [editor_index_adapter]
        [base_registry]
        [register_commands]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/activity-bar/components/WorkspacePane.svelte"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/ideas-summary/components/StatusBar.svelte"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/create-base.test.ts:creates .reqlan marker and reports created"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-refresh.test.ts:refreshBases after createBase registers the new base"]
    )
}

refresh_bases_pass {
    **Refresh bases** is separate from **Refresh index**.
    A bases pass must: (1) prune registered bases whose `.reqlan` marker is gone
    (`existsSync` probe — O(known bases)); (2) register bases from host-supplied marker
    paths (VS Code `findFiles` under `**/.reqlan/**` plus workspace-root probes for empty
    markers). Do **not** walk the workspace tree with `readdir` on Refresh bases.
    Analytical API: [base_registry] `refreshBases` / `pruneMissingBases` /
    `basesFromMarkerPaths`. Editor adapter [editor_index_adapter] `refreshBases` collects
    markers and calls that API without soft-syncing the idea index.
    Triggers: command `reqlan.refreshBases`, Base picker header button, marker create/delete
    watcher, workspace-folder change, and [refresh_bases_on_load].
    Related: [refresh_index_separate], [select_base_dialog], [multi_base_environment],
    ["../extension/features-graph-analysers.rq".indexing_trigger_manual].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [base_registry]
        [base_discovery]
        [editor_index_adapter]
        [register_commands]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/activity-bar/components/BasePicker.svelte"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/ideas-summary/components/StatusBar.svelte"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/activity_bar_module/activity-bar-webview-provider.ts"]
        ["../../packages/extension/src/webview_module/ideas-summary-panel.ts"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-refresh.test.ts:refreshBases registers markers and prunes missing"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-refresh.test.ts:refreshBases rediscovers a nested base from marker paths"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-registry-refresh.test.ts:refreshBases after createBase registers the new base"]
        ["../../packages/analytical/test/base-discovery.test.ts:basesFromMarkerPaths builds descriptors without a tree walk"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:IndexService.refreshBases calls registry.refreshBases"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:IndexService.syncWorkspace does not call registry.refreshBases"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:reqlan.refreshBases command is registered"]
    )
}

refresh_bases_on_load {
    On extension index activate, run one [refresh_bases_pass] in the **background** (do not
    block watcher setup on a tree walk). After the pass settles, soft-sync the active base
    via [refresh_index_separate] when at least one base exists; otherwise prompt
    [create_base_onboarding].
    @implementation (
        [editor_index_adapter]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:IndexService.activate schedules refreshBases"]
    )
    @status done
}

refresh_index_separate {
    Manual **Refresh index** (command `reqlan.refreshIndex`, Workspace / Ideas Summary
    Refresh index buttons) soft-syncs the active base only. It must **not** rediscover
    bases or walk the tree. Clear & rebuild likewise rebuilds the active base without a
    bases rediscovery pass. Use [refresh_bases_pass] when the set of bases may have changed.
    Related: ["../extension/features-graph-analysers.rq".indexing_trigger_manual].

    @status done
    @implementation (
        [editor_index_adapter]
        [register_commands]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/activity-bar/components/WorkspacePane.svelte"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/ideas-summary/components/IndexPanel.svelte"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:IndexService.syncWorkspace does not call registry.refreshBases"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:reqlan.refreshIndex command uses syncWorkspace"]
    )
}

select_base_dialog {
    Users choose the active base via a VS Code QuickPick dialog (command `reqlan.selectBase`,
    Base picker trigger, Ideas Summary base control). The dialog lists discovered bases by
    label/path; picking one pins the active base ([active_base_switch]) without kicking a sync.
    The Base picker header hosts the [refresh_bases_pass] button beside the Base label.
    @implementation (
        ["../../packages/extension/src/analytical_submodule/commands/select-base-dialog.ts"]
        [register_commands]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/activity-bar/components/BasePicker.svelte"]
        ["../../packages/extension/webviews/ideas-summary/components/StatusBar.svelte"]
    )
    @tests (
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:reqlan.selectBase command is registered"]
        ["../../packages/extension/test/refresh-bases-wiring.test.ts:BasePicker posts openSelectBaseDialog and refreshBases"]
    )
    @status done
}

no_base_behaviour {
    When no base is found, the extension should prompt the user to create a base at the workspace-folder root.
    consideration should be made for the [cli_package], the [extension] and the [analysis_scope]
    The indexing should not throw errors - it should default to a global tmp index scope the workspace; or current working directory.
    In the cli; an warning should be shown on first command execution if no base is found.
}

